--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party scanners distributed in the container images
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Toleman orchestrates best-of-breed open-source scanners rather than
reimplementing them. It invokes each as a separate process; none is linked
into Toleman's own code. The published container images
(ghcr.io/toleman-platform/toleman-platform-backend) bundle the binaries and
packages below, each remaining under its own license and copyright:

  Trivy                 Apache License 2.0
                        Copyright Aqua Security Software Ltd.
                        https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy

  gosec                 Apache License 2.0
                        Copyright the gosec authors
                        https://github.com/securego/gosec

  Gitleaks              MIT License
                        Copyright Zachary Rice
                        https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks

  Semgrep               GNU Lesser General Public License v2.1
                        Copyright Semgrep, Inc.
                        https://github.com/semgrep/semgrep

  ModelScan             Apache License 2.0
                        Copyright Protect AI
                        https://github.com/protectai/modelscan

Semgrep is LGPL-2.1 licensed and is bundled unmodified, invoked as a
separate executable. Its source is available at the URL above; nothing in
Toleman's own Apache-2.0 grant restricts your rights under the LGPL with
respect to that component.

Rules run through Semgrep's `--config=auto` are fetched at scan time from
the Semgrep Registry and are governed by Semgrep's own terms, not by this
license. The curated LLM ruleset under backend/app/scanners/rules/ is
Toleman's own work and is covered by LICENSE.

Vulnerability, exploit-prediction and advisory data consumed at runtime --
including the NVD, the CISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog, FIRST's
EPSS scores, and OSV -- are retrieved from their respective providers and
remain subject to those providers' terms of use. Toleman redistributes none
of it.

Python and Node dependencies resolved at build time are not enumerated here;
each carries its own license, recorded in backend/requirements.txt and
frontend/package-lock.json and reported by Toleman's own SBOM output.
